+# Validation-only crossed inference: implementation plan
+
+Spec: reports/diagnostics/error-analysis-20260911/MINIMAL_NEXT_STEP.md. This implements the already authorized next local step. No server access, new training, test-based tuning, or paper edits. Parent owns local evidence preparation, documentation, integration, and GitHub push. Implementation uses a separate worktree; persistent user authorization covers normal final merge/push.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Model source, train.py, trainers, datasets, clip, Dassl, historical checkpoints/configs/reports are immutable. Add only independent tools and targeted tests. Do not instantiate a Trainer: its model builder creates an optimizer. Construct the frozen source's model class directly, set eval and all parameters requires_grad=False, use inference_mode/no_grad. Never create optimizer or invoke backward.
+- Exactly UCF101/DTD/FGVCAircraft, seeds 1/2/3, Base classes and validation split only, existing epoch20 CoOp/KD0/KD1. Main candidate S1+M logits average at alpha0.5; report all combinations, no fitting/search. Preserve T0 and T1 separately even if equal; record exact tensor equality. Only measured values may become results.
+- Inventory at reports/diagnostics/error-analysis-20260911/evidence/proposed-probe-inputs.json fixes 27 checkpoint/manifest hashes, source SHA, train/val sample SHA, CLIP and template hashes. CoOp template null is intentional, KD templates fixed. UCF d74a9770d0d814c56269486e2492327881633d98314281d0f13a584ee279f17f; other two 9bd4a7f248f09c47be17c1bb64921bd9a29d9f3b46e03e8caac9b934b2a95bba. Read own checkpoints only after hash validation. Legacy CoOp declared KD1 vs effectiveKD0 is already recorded; do not generalize permissive matching.
+- Strict val-only: missing/empty val rejects, no test fallback. Validate actual train/val disjoint image identities (resolve symlinks), class/label order and all source sample hashes. Reuse frozen dataset reading/sampling/subsample APIs without invoking constructors that write caches: read fixed splits, seed RNG, sample all-class train16 then val4 in that order, then Base subsample, matching original hashes. For Aircraft use its source reader on a read-only instance without constructor; no new split or input pickle creation. Build actual source evaluation transform/DatasetWrapper/SequentialSampler for only val, workers0. Do not iterate test images. Metadata-only test membership hash checks permitted.
+- Fresh output outside all immutable inputs; never overwrite. Persist protocol, raw FP32 logits, sample IDs/labels/class order, checkpoint/assets/source/tool hashes, effective cfg/transform representation + digest, environment/precision. CUDA required for full export; prepare CPU does not construct CLIP or run inference. Prepare must actually validate loaders and decode all val images when data present. No GPU-ready claim from CPU tests.
+- Use meaningful tests with hand-derived fixtures, missing val, hash/labels/order failure, strict loading, all fusion formulas, non-finite/shape checks, input unchanged/output collision. Run focused tests during iteration and full tests once at completion. No network or package installation needed; Python ../../tc-venv/bin/python, PYTHONPATH=.:Dassl.pytorch, one-thread env.
+
+## Task 1: Implement and test a complete validation export and CPU analysis path
+
+Ownership: new scripts/repro/validation_probe.py, scripts/repro/validation_analysis.py, tests/repro/test_validation_probe.py, tests/repro/test_validation_analysis.py. Add small supporting modules only if needed for a clear split, report rationale. No other product code edits. You are not alone in this codebase: parent owns docs/receipts; never revert others' work. No subagents. Follow TDD: tests fail for missing behavior before implementation; preserve commands/results in report. Commit owned files when complete.
+
+Implement this cohesive local toolset:
+
+1. CLI prepare for one dataset/seed, taking --inventory, --workspace-root (resolves inventory's relative checkpoints), --source-root (matching historical source), --data-root, --output-dir NEW. Source root contains templates and clip/ViT-B-16.pt (parent locates/assets stage separately). Validate inventory case, checkpoint+sidecar+manifest+effective config, epoch/provenance/model signatures, teacher tensor equality and source/assets SHA. All role schemas/losses and sample hashes must match exact expected role; do not trust user-declared signatures alone. Use frozen train.setup_cfg or original configs with explicit supported location/device/val overrides; reject unnoticed protocol changes. Verify code imports really come from requested source (one source tree per CLI process; reject module contamination). Source scripts may differ; use actual source model modules rather than new copies.
+2. Read fixed official dataset metadata and regenerate historical sampled Base train/val lists through frozen APIs (no cache writes). Match all roles' recorded train/val/test digests. Validate real image existence, unique identities, labels/classnames and disjoint train/val; record source metadata hashes, sample inventory and decoded deterministic val transform evidence. Save standalone prepared.json in fresh output; all preparatory work CPU only and no CLIP construction. No fallback if actual data missing; metadata-only check must not masquerade as prepare success. Prepared command/protocol allows subsequent export after deployment/relocation by rerunning prepare at destination, not editing receipts.
+3. CLI export --prepared FILE --output-dir NEW (always CUDA; no CPU inference fallback). Revalidate prepared inputs and data/transform identities before expensive model load and after evaluation. Construct source's CoOp_TextConsistency_Ablation model class directly; manually strict-load nn.ModuleDict of prompt/aggregator without silent missing/unexpected/wrong shape keys. Base classes are same as training; class-dependent token buffers must agree with rebuilt CLIP/class order or be explicitly verified before excluding, never silently ignored. Record actual model forward precision. All model weights frozen. Use same val batch across roles and identical images; compare frozen image features/logit scale shared properties or compute once correctly from frozen source. Export C,S0,S1,M,T0,T1 as finite float32 [N,C] arrays plus labels in an NPZ without object/pickle arrays, JSON row identity and metadata/hash receipts. M must exactly use frozen_fusion_logits's masked normalized descriptor mean, with historical CLIP scale; both T branches retained even identical. Preserve original full-model forward semantics. If a more efficient shared implementation is used, test equality against source direct forwards on a small CLIP-like fixture. Do not need full CLIP CPU inference during this task. Failures record failure, never success or partial metric mislabeled complete.
+4. CPU analysis CLI validates export status/NPZ/file hashes/schema/sample and class alignment/finite shapes, then produces all raw branch metrics and every C/S0/S1 x M/T0/T1 pair's fixed logits/probability half fusion (18 combos), no search. Report accuracy, NLL, multiclass Brier (sum over classes mean samples), probability top1-top2 margin (name explicit), all student-vs-teacher error overlap/disagreement and paired rescue/harm comparisons vs C. Stable numerical softmax/log-softmax; no arbitrary clipping making confidence metrics misleading. Save counts and predictions for complete audit, not only highest score.
+5. Aggregate complete nine-case analysis only after validating unique dataset/seed coverage, val/Base/protocol/source/assets/checkpoint provenance and compatible settings; use three seeds per dataset and equal dataset weighting. Apply exactly the MINIMAL_NEXT_STEP fixed budget guards (candidate S1+M logits vs C+M logits and probability, macro difference >=0 and each dataset mean delta >=-1pp; candidate vs S0+M macro >0). Report all dataset/seed values, means and sample SD; no HM/Novel claim, no significance assertion, and no automatic training action. Duplicated T branches must not double-weight datasets/guards. Missing/duplicate case or mixed config/source raises rather than silently aggregating.
+
+Tests should exercise real functions with temporary files and tiny real torch modules/images. Mock only unavailable CLIP/CUDA boundaries, not assertions on mock existence. At least one end-to-end synthetic artifact->analysis->nine-case aggregation verifies outputs/guards and failure cases independently of implementation formulas; negative cases include permuted classes/samples, omitted role parameters, hash mismatch and already-existing output. Tests must show optimizer creation/backward would fail if invoked by export. Small tests don't establish actual CUDA parity; label that pending in report.
+
+Report full implementation, tests/red-green evidence, commit SHA, any unresolved limitations to this plan's task-1-report.md. Return brief status/commit/test summary only. Ask controller for concrete missing input rather than guessing protocol.
+
+## Execution status
+
+Task 1 implementation and one fix round completed on `1406ca3`; task re-review approved all four fixes. Focused17/full127 tests and all9 real CPU preparations passed, plus explicit no-CUDA export rejection and immutable input checks. See [preparation report](../../reports/preparation/validation-probe-20260911/README.md). Final whole-branch review pending; real CUDA export remains a separate unexecuted phase. No server access, new training, measured method result, or paper change.
